This looks like January 2014. Unemployment was 6.7% (December 2013 reading, published in January 2014; the January reading was 6.6%). The 10-year yield was 2.72% and the fed funds rate 0.07%. US equities fell 3.5% in the month, which matches January 2014, as do emerging-market equities dropping 8.6% and gold's 12-month return of -25.5%. Long Treasuries gained 6.3% in the month, also consistent with January 2014.

Unemployment of 6.7% fits December 2013 or January 2014. The 3-month change of -0.5 fits too: October 2013 was 7.2% and January 2014 was 6.6%. Taking the 6.7% as the latest published value, the snapshot is probably end of January 2014, since the January report came out in early February. At end of January, the latest published value would be December's 6.7%.

